     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "[Followup from Sourceforge Tracker]",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Followup Submitter: fcswa",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Logged In: YES ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "user_id=1855086",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Originator: NO",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "We need to develop a set of use cases to better characterize this item.  On the one hand this may be a kind of agility for BMECH bindings which permits variable numbers, kinds, or types in calling parameters.  Especially for types this is consistent with the CMDA notion of models.  This may also work for cardinality where a BMECH is bound to a variable number of similar parameters (like having one chapter of a book in each datastream - the number of chapters vary between books).",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
